        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "d45ef8d8-7875-3b04-a70d-8b5cf160226c",
                "word": "rétropropulsion",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9cb0cfbb-beec-4321-8384-28b34be2658a",
                        "entry_id": "d45ef8d8-7875-3b04-a70d-8b5cf160226c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "rétropropulsions"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "0ec1409f-bac1-4a1f-b0cd-69c28d63f873",
                        "entry_id": "d45ef8d8-7875-3b04-a70d-8b5cf160226c",
                        "tags": [
                            "orthographe traditionnelle"
                        ],
                        "form": "rétro-propulsion"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6dc04b8d-8b25-3d7b-b4d9-4408c9ad5236",
                        "entry_id": "d45ef8d8-7875-3b04-a70d-8b5cf160226c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Marche arrière."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3014009d-43be-4e00-9843-161b903943f9",
                                "sense_id": "6dc04b8d-8b25-3d7b-b4d9-4408c9ad5236",
                                "text": "Fais reculer ton kayak sur vingt mètres en utilisant la rétropropulsion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9edec2c-66f8-48ef-975d-c1371142ff68",
                                "sense_id": "6dc04b8d-8b25-3d7b-b4d9-4408c9ad5236",
                                "text": "Le plus petit oiseau du monde, le colibri, est aussi le seul à connaître tout à la fois le vol stationnaire et la rétropropulsion."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "04a92f31-985f-3853-8b3f-14cd2341d31d",
                        "entry_id": "d45ef8d8-7875-3b04-a70d-8b5cf160226c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Freinage d'un véhicule à l'aide de propulseur orienté dans le sens inverse du mouvement du véhicule."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "71466bff-db46-47f5-ab66-2e95c7cbdee3",
                                "sense_id": "04a92f31-985f-3853-8b3f-14cd2341d31d",
                                "text": "Le freinage d'un engin spatial se fait par rétropropulsion à l'aide de rétrofusées."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8be9d9bf-5fe2-406c-81bd-a3d6974c6c6a",
                                "sense_id": "04a92f31-985f-3853-8b3f-14cd2341d31d",
                                "text": "Une brève secousse en même temps que le grondement sourd des réacteurs en rétropropulsion les avertit qu’ils venaient de se poser."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fd4b452d-8095-4eea-8c85-87b40dde9856",
                        "source_entry_id": "d45ef8d8-7875-3b04-a70d-8b5cf160226c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Sens 1",
                        "target_lang_word": "retropropulsion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "retropropulsion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5dcda2fc-1272-30c7-a0ac-061c2c82b0d4",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b6ac9-6266-3f62-a277-9df3f763b6cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Backward propulsion, especially the use of rockets to brake or change direction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78836083-b970-4620-9d27-f9a5fa441efe",
                                                "sense_id": "5dcda2fc-1272-30c7-a0ac-061c2c82b0d4",
                                                "text": "Recent studies have concluded that Viking-era entry system deceleration technologies are extremely difficult to scale for progressively larger payloads (tens of metric tons) required for human Mars exploration. Supersonic retropropulsion is one of a few developing technologies that may enable future human-scale Mars entry systems."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93a1c27f-b0f4-3abc-ba8e-c9cd8a74f2ef",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b6ac9-6266-3f62-a277-9df3f763b6cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of retropulsion (“abnormal tendency to step backwards”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8d3e149-3eb7-4987-9bfb-4524b267d120",
                                                "sense_id": "93a1c27f-b0f4-3abc-ba8e-c9cd8a74f2ef",
                                                "text": "At the autopsy Pierret found sclerosis of the columns of Goll, and he thinks that disease of these columns explains the tendency to propulsion and retropropulsion experienced by the patient as well as the uncertainty felt in maintaining the erect posture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afd449c4-80cc-4ca6-a127-ab3dce5cb922",
                                                "sense_id": "93a1c27f-b0f4-3abc-ba8e-c9cd8a74f2ef",
                                                "text": "There was complete loss of automatic associated movements with lateropropulsion and retropropulsion to a degree rarely so complete in the juvenile form of parkinsonian disease."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aeb14e3a-4850-4f4f-b86d-9e8ca1674c1a",
                                                "sense_id": "93a1c27f-b0f4-3abc-ba8e-c9cd8a74f2ef",
                                                "text": "‘This 80-year-old woman has Parkinson’s disease. Please assess the severity of the condition.’ […] It is probably a little dangerous to look for propulsion or retropropulsion (see Table 15.57)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "741d494b-f2c3-3595-a6e0-26c7e269f10b",
                                        "entry_id": "c99b6ac9-6266-3f62-a277-9df3f763b6cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of retropulsion (“forcing something to move backwards or inwards”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bc7a711-ad15-4c9a-b865-30b1cfde80bb",
                                                "sense_id": "741d494b-f2c3-3595-a6e0-26c7e269f10b",
                                                "text": "Also, the retropropulsion of blood through the mitral valve caused a “gyration” of the heart at each beat; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64eb3dd8-2281-410a-9afd-1b9794c7e434",
                                                "sense_id": "741d494b-f2c3-3595-a6e0-26c7e269f10b",
                                                "text": "Relative indications for surgery include: […] radiological evidence of spinal instability, complete vertebral collapse or retropropulsion of bone fragments […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21210a63-ac1a-4b57-9aa4-1d2788b079c2",
                                                "sense_id": "741d494b-f2c3-3595-a6e0-26c7e269f10b",
                                                "text": "Be aware also that the mandibular support of the tongue may be compromised in jaw fractures and can easily obstruct the airway, in addition to soft tissue swelling and retropropulsion of mid-face fractures."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "213e3ec3-35e8-49bb-a3f2-73fddf98e8af",
                        "source_entry_id": "d45ef8d8-7875-3b04-a70d-8b5cf160226c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Sens 1",
                        "target_lang_word": "retropulsion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "retropulsion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3351c525-78f6-3d21-bb0e-af44645fc80e",
                                        "entry_id": "621d8e89-73bf-3998-a516-c257bbdc378f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tendency to step or walk backwards involuntarily, especially as a symptom of parkinsonism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0adc3f6b-1e76-4236-ab00-08599daaebb7",
                                                "sense_id": "3351c525-78f6-3d21-bb0e-af44645fc80e",
                                                "text": "Retropulsion most often occurs when you are trying to reach for something higher than sholder level."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e22139a-7d6e-447c-aaa4-26e0862ceb83",
                                                "sense_id": "3351c525-78f6-3d21-bb0e-af44645fc80e",
                                                "text": "For patients prone to retropulsion, wearing shoes with high heels may diminish or prevent the backward stepping."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "930b0b06-029f-41ea-8dc1-80e1355009ee",
                                                "sense_id": "3351c525-78f6-3d21-bb0e-af44645fc80e",
                                                "text": "Pretreating rats with α-methyl-ρ-tyrosine (30 mg/kg i.p. at -4 h) to interrupt the synthesis of catecholamines antagonized pivoting and retropulsion induced by levallorphan (50 mg/kg i.p.) (WRAY 1973) but, surprisingly, not lateral head movements and pivoting elicited by cyclazocine (3 mg/kg s.c.) (BUCKETT and SHAW 1975)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b0dec6a1-f643-36d6-8943-3de54fa9b4ce",
                                        "entry_id": "621d8e89-73bf-3998-a516-c257bbdc378f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The pushing or forcing of something to move backwards or inwards."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12d2fd6e-4b06-4d80-8e78-efbe2ef98154",
                                                "sense_id": "b0dec6a1-f643-36d6-8943-3de54fa9b4ce",
                                                "text": "Retropulsion of the eye slackens the rectus muscle and, if forced ductions improve with retropulsion, then the restriction is secondary to a tight rectus muscle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbde9b0a-92c8-4a05-95e5-2cc9fa26d05a",
                                                "sense_id": "b0dec6a1-f643-36d6-8943-3de54fa9b4ce",
                                                "text": "Spinal CT or MRI reveals violation of the posterior cortex of the vertebral bodies (burst fracture) with retropulsion of bone into the spinal canal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82220102-c500-41db-9d48-011d4965357a",
                                                "sense_id": "b0dec6a1-f643-36d6-8943-3de54fa9b4ce",
                                                "text": "The goal of retropulsion is to expand the diameter of the urethra with fluid to suspend the obstructing substance in a fluid column that will carry it back into the bladder."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "704b090c-50d8-4d4f-a81a-6ecddb978664",
                                                "sense_id": "b0dec6a1-f643-36d6-8943-3de54fa9b4ce",
                                                "text": "The motility of the gastroduodenal junction regulates gastric emptying and minimises retropulsion of the duodenal contents into the antrum."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7f29c57-606c-3457-90d5-94468f5eed15",
                                        "entry_id": "621d8e89-73bf-3998-a516-c257bbdc378f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Transfer of a disease from an external source to an internal organ."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12939ae8-9085-464b-8622-b75e1aad6c64",
                                                "sense_id": "b7f29c57-606c-3457-90d5-94468f5eed15",
                                                "text": "From this account, it will also be evident, that there can be no danger from the retropulsion, or rather the retiring of prickly heat, except what may arise from the cause that checked perspiration. Many absurd notions have been entertained on this subject, which have really proved prejudicial to health. It hs been very generally supposed, that the matter of prickly heat was highly injurious, and therefore, that the retiring of it into the body was extremely dangerous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15320b87-e739-4c33-9a00-1a98768aa886",
                                                "sense_id": "b7f29c57-606c-3457-90d5-94468f5eed15",
                                                "text": "The arthritic blepharoblenorrhœa and ophthalmoblenorrhœa appear only as a real metastasis of gout, having always followed its retropulsion in the great toe, from the application of cold moisture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "934424d5-a254-460d-a0fb-dbd62184faf9",
                                                "sense_id": "b7f29c57-606c-3457-90d5-94468f5eed15",
                                                "text": "And hence dry asthma, like the preceding, as thus diversified by its occasional causes, may be contemplated under the following varieties: ... From retropulsion of some acrid humour from the surface of the body."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9a5cc751-acfe-4f0f-b90e-9d9a83d8c2a9",
